      "url": "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/how-movie-star-james-stewart-became-a-war-hero",
      "category": "uncategorized",
      "checkedAt": "2026-11-10T21:25:15.804Z",
      "httpStatus": 200,
      "finalUrl": "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/how-movie-star-james-stewart-became-a-war-hero/",
      "contentType": "text/html; charset=UTF-8",
      "pageTitle": "How movie star James Stewart became a war hero - CBS News",
      "pageDescription": "In 1941 the Oscar-winning actor answered his nation",
      "evidenceText": "How movie star James Stewart became a war hero - CBS News Watch CBS News It's trite but true; Jimmy Stewart played the Everyman better than everyone. He had the gawky innocence to be an idealistic senator, in \"Mr. Smith Goes to Washington\"; an eccentric with a six-foot-tall rabbit pal in \"Harvey\"; and a depth, in \"Rear Window\" and \"Vertigo,\" that even Alfred Hitchcock found mysterious. But it was director Frank Capra who gave us the Jimmy Stewart that everyone still depends on every Christmas. \"It's a Wonderful Life\" is remarkable for a lot of reasons, not the least of which is that Stewart's memorable performance was his first after an almost-five-year absence from Hollywood. Audiences hadn't seen him on screen since 1941, the same year he took home the Academy Award for \"The Philadelphia Story.\" He was a Hollywood A-lister. But not long after, he found himself on another list: the list for the draft . Stewart could have served safely stateside doing recruiting films and such. But he wanted, or at least felt, he needed to do more. Already an accomplished pilot, Stewart enlisted in the Army Air Corps. \"He knew that America needed good pilots; he was one,\" said Janie McKirgan, curator at the Jimmy Stewart Museum in his hometown of Indiana, Pennsylvania. Lt. Gen. Valin, Chief of Staff, French Air Force, awards the Croix De Guerre With Palm to Col. James Stewart for exceptional services in the liberation, 1944. U.S. Air Force McKirgan said few wanted to let Hollywood's golden boy actually fly: \"It took a long time for him to find somebody in the Army Air Corps that was willing to take that risk,\" she said. \"Because if Jimmy Stewart, Academy Award-winning Jimmy Stewart, got shot down, it would be a huge blow to troop morale, to America, to everything.\" His fight to be able to fight despite his celebrity is the subject of a new film out this week, called \"Jimmy.\" It stars Max Casella as director Frank Capra, and K.J. Apa as Jimmy Stewart. \"We really set out to make the movie that Frank and Jimmy never got to make,\" Apa said. Casella said he was only vaguely aware of Stewart's wartime service; Apa did not know about it: \"I can't believe it was true,\" he said. \"It was the courage that made me dumbfounded of his story.\" Casella said, \"He gave up Hollywood at the very top of the mountain.\" To watch a trailer for \"Jimmy\" click on the video player below: JIMMY Official Trailer 2 (2026) KJ Apa by FilmSelect on YouTube There'a a lot of what you'd want in the film: Old Hollywood, action-packed air battles. But really at its heart, this is a movie about what Stewart's service did to his soul. Stewart flew 20 combat missions over Germany. He lost men, and saw things he wished he didn't. But like most of that generation, he kept those horrors to himself. \"Dad never talked about his military service to us,\" said Kelly Stewart Harcourt, one of his twin daughters. \"Never talked about his war service at all.\" Harcourt, an executive producer on the film, says her dad came home from war a different man: \"He said, 'I'm an out-of-work actor and an out-of-work pilot, and I don't know what I'm gonna do. Do I even want to make films again?'\" Her dad kept a diary, something she and her sister found in his nightstand after he passed away in 1997. She read from it, having never shared it publicly: \"This was a terrible day. We lost 13 crews out of the group on the mission today. Only half of them came back.\" The next day, though, in the see-saw of war, everyone came home safely. That was a cause for celebration.  And yet, Stewart wrote this: \"It's strange that this could practically cancel out the loss of all those boys, but I guess that's the way things have to be in this god-damn, stupid, lousy, dirty war.\" Harcourt says her dad suffered from nightmares, depression, anxiety &ndash; symptoms that would be diagnosed as PTSD today.  And that, in a way, is what gets us back to \"It's a Wonderful Life.\" \"Dear Father in heaven, I'm not a praying man but, if You're up there and You can hear me, show me the way...\" Jimmy Stewart as George Bailey in Frank Capra's \"It's a Wonderful Life.\"  RKO Radio Pictures For years there had been quiet speculation that whatever demons Stewart may have brought home were exorcised in the role of George Bailey, a desperate man also pushed to the edge. Harcourt believes he brought those feelings to the role of Bailey. \"You can't pull off that performance without feeling like that,\" she said. We'll never know, of course.  Whatever his muse, its effect was unforgettable. Stewart went on to do more than 50 films after \"It's a Wonderful Life.\" But he was most proud of his service to his country. In 1983, Stewart was honored at the Kennedy Center, where cadets from the U.S. Air Force Academy brought him near tears. Jimmy Stewart did indeed have a wonderful life, but his sacrifice, and those of others, gave us a pretty wonderful life, too. Web extra: Filming Jimmy Stewart and Donna Reed's \"It's a Wonderful Life\" kiss (Video) Hollywood historian Sam Wasson, author of the biography \"Frank Capra: A Life,\" talks with Lee Cowan about Jimmy Stewart and Donna Reed's emotional performance in Capra's 1946 classic \"It's a Wonderful Life,\" and how the director created a timeless classic &ndash; even if it wasn't the box office giant he'd hoped for. Web extra: Filming Jimmy Stewart and Donna Reed's \"It's a Wonderful Life\" kiss 03:00 Read an excerpt: \"Frank Capra: A Life\" by Sam Wasson       Story produced by David Rothman. Editor: Remington Korper.  See also:  The enduring message of \"It's a Wonderful Life\" (\"Sunday Morning\")     For more info: \"Jimmy\" opens in theaters Nov. 6 Author Sam Wasson \"Frank Capra: A Life\" by Sam Wasson (HarperCollins), in Hardcover, eBook and Audio formats, available via Amazon , Barnes & Noble and Bookshop.org The Jimmy Stewart Museum , Indiana, Pa. Movies More DOC NYC documentary film festival returns. Check out this year's lineup. Judi Dench on an actor's life Extended interview: Dame Judi Dench and Brendan O'Hea Book excerpt: \"Is It Too Late to Make a Run For It?\" by Judi Dench with Brendan O'Hea Filming Jimmy Stewart and Donna Reed's \"It's a Wonderful Life\" kiss Go deeper with The Free Press The Dems Won Congress, Martha Stewart Lost Halloween, and J-Law Has a Whole New Face Kristen Stewart Needs You to Know She Thinks Method Acting Is Cringe \"Jimmy\": How movie star James Stewart became a war hero 08:36 \"Jimmy\": How movie star James Stewart became a war hero (08:36) \"The Altruists\" actor Julia Garner on surprising herself Read a free excerpt from Oprah Winfrey's book club pick: \"Solace in Winter\" by Mary Lawson Dad who stopped Oregon school shooting details moment he killed gunman: \"He had taken the lives of innocent little babies\" The Dems Won Congress, Martha Stewart Lost Halloween, and J-Law Has a Whole New Face View CBS News In CBS News App Open Chrome Safari Continue <path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M6.0152 0C7.66926 0 9.0829 0.5856 10.2558 1.75698C11.4286 2.92839 12.0149 4.34027 12.0149 5.99228C12.0149 7.65515 11.4287 9.07181 10.2558 10.2422C9.0829 11.4126 7.6693 11.9985 6.0152 12C4.36114 12 2.94492 11.4144 1.7669 10.243C0.588909 9.07161 0 7.6549 0 5.99311C0 4.34106 0.588884 2.92921 1.7669 1.75779C2.94492 0.586387 4.36114 0.000531171 6.0152 0ZM37.8085 0.350908C40.197 0.350908 41.4373 1.80037 41.453 1.81878L39.906 3.36839C39.906 3.36839 39.1323 2.441 37.8891 2.4409C36.7286 2.4409 36.2602 2.90474 36.2602 3.52291C36.2605 5.38104 41.689 4.52739 41.6891 8.32422C41.6891 10.1061 40.1416 11.6556 37.5784 11.6556C34.7906 11.6547 33.3941 9.95902 33.3875 9.95107L34.9391 8.40553C34.9497 8.41869 35.8767 9.56438 37.4983 9.56438C38.736 9.56438 39.2822 9.02368 39.2823 8.3283C39.2823 6.4699 33.8533 7.32363 33.8533 3.52657C33.8533 1.822 35.3235 0.350908 37.8085 0.350908ZM18.9787 0.346029C22.003 0.346029 23.5544 2.5145 23.5544 2.5145L22.0032 4.05964C21.