      "evidenceText": "International Fact-Checking Network - Poynter International Fact-Checking Network - Poynter DONATE What do you want to search? Submit Sign In | Membership News Training Ethics Fact-Checking Media Literacy AI Events Future of Public Media Newmark Ethics Center IFCN MediaWise PolitiFact Donate About Us Press Freedom Watch The Poynter 50 Podcasts Artificial Intelligence Business & Work Reporting & Editing Fact-Checking Ethics & Trust Local News Journalism, Media & Communication Training Poynter Membership Categories Consulting & Coaching For ACES Members For Local News Funders All Categories Broadcast & Visual Journalism Business & Work Ethics Fact-Checking & Media Literacy Leadership Reporting & Editing Writing Poynter ACES Introductory Certificate in Editing Poynter ACES Intermediate Certificate in Editing Poynter ACES Advanced Certificate in Editing Workshops and Coaching Tools for Funders Ethics Ethics Training Ethics Articles AI Ethics Public Editor Project Get Ethics Advice Fact-Checking Articles IFCN IFCN Grants International Fact-Checking Day Teen Creator Network PolitiFact MediaWise Media Literacy Resources AI Literacy Ambassadors Teen Creator Network Research & News International en Español MediaWise Training All Events The 2026 Poynter Journalism Prizes What is the International Fact-Checking Network? The International Fact-Checking Network (IFCN) at Poynter connects and strengthens fact-checking around the world. Founded in 2015, the IFCN advocates for information integrity and supports fact-checking journalists through networking, capacity building and collaboration. IFCN connects more than 170 fact-checking organizations worldwide through outreach, training and global events. Our team monitors trends in fact-checking to contribute to public knowledge and media literacy, and to provide support for new projects and initiatives that advance accountability in journalism. Grant Opportunities For fact-checkers seeking fellowships or funding to launch your next big idea. See if you're eligible for support Code of Principles For organizations that aspire to abide by our commitment to fact-checking excellence. Read our pledge to facts GlobalFact The world’s largest annual conference to convene fact-checkers, share resources and explore the field’s future. Be part of the discussion Transparency Build trust in the IFCN that fosters global collaboration with certainty. Read our Transparency Statement Training and Resources Master the art of fact-checking and improve your media literacy skills. Learn from our experts CoronavirusFacts Alliance Unite with fact-checkers around the world to publish the truth about COVID-19. Fight the infodemic IFCN condemns coordinated attacks on Faktoje of Albania Attacks leave out context and mischaracterize funding influence November 2, 2026 The International Fact-Checking Network Opinion | Fact-checking isn’t just for journalists. Here are 5 reasons it’s for you, too Fact-checking makes you a clearer communicator, a better decision-maker and a more trusted friend. A new course helps you learn how September 28, 2026 Angie Drobnic Holan World’s fact-checkers to meet in Antwerp, Belgium, for GlobalFact 2027 Home to 170 nationalities, the port city is a short train ride from Brussels, where EU institutions shape Europe’s platform rules September 17, 2026 The International Fact-Checking Network Statement from the International Fact-Checking Network on Meta’s expansion of Community Notes to Latin America Substituting community notes for professional fact-checking will result in a degraded information environment September 9, 2026 The International Fact-Checking Network US fact-checkers launch collaboration debunking deceptive 2026 midterm ads and election disinformation A newsletter aimed at media, content creators and election observers will analyze messages and trends in midterm elections and voting August 20, 2026 The International Fact-Checking Network More Articles A newsletter about fact-checking misinformation and getting at the truth Factually Subscribe Subscribe to Factually Advertisement",
