      "pageDescription": "With the EU banning “nudifier” apps in one month, our latest investigation has uncovered a network behind the publication of hundreds of such apps, promoted by thousands of pornographic ads on Meta. \n\nAt the beginning of September, we discovered an operation behind over 400+ nudifier apps published on Google Play and the Apple App Store.",
      "evidenceText": "Advertised by Design: A Network of Nudify Apps | AI Forensics Advertised by Design: A Network of Nudify Apps Subscribe Nudify Apps on Meta, Google Play and the App Store 02-11-2026 Download Report Project overview Share This Project : With the EU banning “nudifier” apps in one month, our latest investigation has uncovered a network behind the publication of hundreds of such apps, promoted by thousands of pornographic ads on Meta. At the beginning of September, we discovered an operation behind over 400+ nudifier apps published on Google Play and the Apple App Store. To avoid detection, these apps disguise themselves as legitimate (a hair salon or outfit swap). But when the user installs it through a Meta ad, the app becomes sexually explicit, with ready-made abuse templates. Since January 1, 2026, over 84k ads matching the network pattern have been distributed on Meta. These ads have been paid for under self-declared and plainly fictitious payer names such as \"123456\". Despite being “reviewed” before publication, the ads are typically illustrated with pornographic content, which violates Meta’s policy. These apps rely on third-party inference providers such as ClothOff’s, Tencent’s, and Shengshu Technology’s models. Featured On 02-11-2026 We helped track down the operator behind the network of 400+ nudifier apps on Google Play and the Apple App Store, promoted by thousands of Meta ads. read article AI Forensics is proud to be trusted by",
