      "evidenceText": "Organized Crime and Corruption Reporting Project | Membership Benefits With a monthly donation of $25, you  join a  community of professionals and engaged citizens  who believe in holding power to account. But your support can go even further — larger contributions help OCCRP uncover corruption, expose organized crime, and protect investigative journalists working on the front lines. Questions How long will I retain access to these benefits if I donate? OCCRP memberships last for 12 months, beginning on the date of your first contribution. If you give monthly, your membership is valid through the last month of your last donation. To cancel your membership at any time, please contact membership@occrp.org . Are donations tax-deductible? OCCRP is a 501(c)(3) tax-exempt organization and your donation may be tax-deductible. Consult your tax advisor. What is OCCRP’s EIN? 26-0898750 Are there other ways to give to OCCRP? If you’d rather not give online, you can mail us a check. Please send it to: OCCRP, 1220 L St. NW Ste 100 #497. Washington, DC 20005. For wire transfers and other charitable giving vehicles, please contact Filip Medic at filip.medic@occrp.org . © 2025 OCCRP           Privacy Policy           Responsible Disclosure           Contact Us If you have further questions or comments, please contact membership@occrp.org . Become an Advocate $25/month Access to members-only OCCRP Briefings, incl. recordings of past events   Participation in members-only surveys on editorial priorities Early access to OCCRP jobs & volunteer opportunities Advocate Help us expose the truth — and access exclusive benefits. Investigative journalism needs allies. Every dollar strengthens independent journalism that governments can’t silence , corporations can’t buy, and the corrupt fear. Become an OCCRP   member today, unlock a range of exclusive benefits, and help put a spotlight on what others want to hide.  Become a Guardian Exclusive Access to members-only OCCR